{
  "id": "al10",
  "title": "Logic",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al10-l1",
      "title": "AND, OR, XOR",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The 8080 can combine bytes bit by bit. ANA r (2 4 r) keeps a 1 only where both A and r have a 1 (AND). ORA r (2 6 r) gives a 1 where either has one (OR). XRA r (2 5 r) gives a 1 where they differ (exclusive OR).",
        "Each of the 8 bits is worked out on its own, like 8 tiny calculations side by side.",
        "With numbers instead of registers: ANI (346), ORI (366) and XRI (356)."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "074   ;      60",
          "076   ; 002: MVI A",
          "125   ;      85",
          "240   ; 004: ANA B",
          "323   ; 005: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "076   ; 007: MVI A",
          "125   ;      85",
          "260   ; 011: ORA B",
          "323   ; 012: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "076   ; 014: MVI A",
          "125   ;      85",
          "250   ; 016: XRA B",
          "323   ; 017: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 021: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○●○●○○ = 20",
          "LEDS ○●●●●●○● = 125",
          "LEDS ○●●○●○○● = 105"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al10-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is 1100 AND 1010?",
          "options": [
            "1000",
            "1110",
            "0110",
            "0010"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Only the leftmost bit is 1 in both."
        },
        {
          "id": "al10-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is 1100 OR 1010?",
          "options": [
            "1110",
            "1000",
            "0110",
            "1111"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1 wherever either has a 1."
        },
        {
          "id": "al10-l1-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is 1100 XOR 1010?",
          "options": [
            "0110",
            "1110",
            "1000",
            "0000"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1 where they differ."
        },
