    {
      "id": "al10-l2",
      "title": "Masks",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A mask is a byte that picks out bits. ANI 00001111 clears the upper four bits and keeps the lower four.",
        "ORI with a mask turns bits on and leaves the others alone: ORI 10000000 switches on the top light.",
        "To test a single bit, AND it out and look at the zero flag: ANI 00000001 then JZ means \"jump if bit 0 is off\". That's also how you test if a number is even."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "266   ;      182",
          "346   ; 002: ANI",
          "017   ;      15",
          "323   ; 004: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "366   ; 006: ORI",
          "200   ;      128",
          "323   ; 010: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 012: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○●●○ = 6",
          "LEDS ●○○○○●●○ = 134"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al10-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does ANI 11110000 do?",
          "options": [
            "Clears the lower 4 bits, keeps the upper 4",
            "Sets the upper 4 bits",
            "Flips all bits",
            "Clears A"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "AND with 0 clears, AND with 1 keeps."
        },
        {
          "id": "al10-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which instruction turns on bit 7 and leaves the rest?",
          "options": [
            "ORI 10000000",
            "ANI 10000000",
            "XRI 01111111",
            "MVI A 10000000"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "OR with 1 sets, OR with 0 keeps."
        },
        {
          "id": "al10-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How do you check if A is even?",
          "options": [
            "ANI 1, then the zero flag is set if it's even",
            "CPI 2",
            "ADD A",
            "ORI 1"
