    {
      "id": "al10-l3",
      "title": "Flipping Bits",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "XRI with a mask flips exactly the bits that are 1 in the mask. XRI 11111111 flips every bit (that's what CMA, 057, does too).",
        "Flipping twice brings everything back: perfect for blinking lights.",
        "XRA A (257) is a quick way to clear A: anything XOR itself is 0. 8080 programmers used it all the time because it's one byte instead of two."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "017   ;      15",
          "323   ; 002: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "356   ; 004: XRI",
          "377   ;      255",
          "323   ; 006: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "356   ; 010: XRI",
          "377   ;      255",
          "323   ; 012: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "257   ; 014: XRA A",
          "323   ; 015: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 017: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○●●●● = 15",
          "LEDS ●●●●○○○○ = 240",
          "LEDS ○○○○●●●● = 15",
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○○ = 0"
        ]
      },
